ntire French scientific community, can locate earthquakes or determine the structure of underwater layers. Deployed at sea up to six kilometers deep, they can record seismic waves for almost a year. For more information: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://parc-obs.insu.cnrs.fr/spip.php?article130\">https://parc-obs.insu.cnrs.fr/spip.php?article130</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"23 May 2012 (upload date)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Olivier Dugornay (Ifremer)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]}}}}